{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"afa050ae-012a-41af-92e6-49ad7c357cb5","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Let's solve two x plus three is less than seven. We want all values of x that make this statement true.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"problem","region":"A1","latex":"2x+3<7"},{"op":"figure","id":"numberline","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3,5],"y":[-1,1],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"axis","from":[-2.7,0],"to":[4.7,0],"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","from":[0,-0.08],"to":[0,0.08]},{"kind":"text","at":[0,-0.35],"text":"0"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,-0.08],"to":[2,0.08]},{"kind":"text","at":[2,-0.35],"text":"2"},{"kind":"text","at":[4.6,-0.35],"text":"x"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"afa050ae-012a-41af-92e6-49ad7c357cb5","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Subtract three from both sides. Then divide by positive two. Neither operation reverses the inequality, so x is less than two.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"subtract","anchor":{"el":"problem","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"2x<4"},{"op":"equation","id":"solution","anchor":{"el":"subtract","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x<2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"afa050ae-012a-41af-92e6-49ad7c357cb5","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Two is the boundary, but it is not included. Draw an open circle at two and an arrow left for all smaller numbers.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"solution_marks","on":"numberline","marks":[{"kind":"circle","id":"boundary","center":[2,0],"r":0.12},{"kind":"segment","from":[1.88,0],"to":[-2.6,0],"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[-0.8,0.55],"text":"x < 2"}]},{"op":"text","id":"excluded","anchor":{"el":"solution","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Open circle: 2 excluded"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Does x = 2 satisfy the original inequality? Why?","expected_gist":"No. Substitution gives 7 < 7, which is false; the boundary is excluded."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"afa050ae-012a-41af-92e6-49ad7c357cb5","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Check one shaded value: x equals zero gives three less than seven. The leftward arrow represents every solution, not just whole numbers.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"check_point","on":"numberline","marks":[{"kind":"point","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.85],"text":"check: 0"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"check_work","anchor":{"el":"excluded","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x=0:\\quad 2(0)+3=3<7\\;\\checkmark"}],"checkpoint":null}}
